      "problem": "Solve for $x,$ if $-\\dfrac{3}{4}x = 12.$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we multiply both sides by $\\color{blue}4$ to get rid of the fraction:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{3}{4}x & =12 \\\\ 4\\cdot (-\\frac{3}{4}x) & =4\\cdot 12 \\\\ \\cancel{4}\\cdot (-\\frac{3}{\\cancel{4}}x) & =48 \\\\ -3x & =48\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we divide both sides of the equation by ${\\color{red}-3}$ to isolate $x\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-3x & =48 \\\\ \\frac{-3x}{-3} & =\\frac{48}{-3} \\\\ \\frac{\\cancel{-3}x}{\\cancel{-3}} & =-16 \\\\ x & =-16\\end{aligned}\n$$",
